<HeadLayout title="How to Back Up Save Data Without Cloud Storage">
  <h1>How to Back Up Save Data Without Cloud Storage</h1>

  <h2>PlayStation 5:</h2>

  <p>
    PS5 <b>does not support</b> exporting individual game save data to external storage.
    However, you can back up all saved data including Monster Hunter Wilds'. Learn
    how to <a
      href="https://www.playstation.com/en-us/support/hardware/back-up-ps5-data-USB/"
      >here</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Xbox Series X|S:</h2>

  <p>
    Xbox Series X|S <b>does not support</b> external backups for game save data. It
    only does so for the games themselves, apps, media, and console settings.
  </p>

  <h2>PC:</h2>

  <p>
    PC players can manually back up their local save files to an external
    storage device.

    <h3>To create a backup:</h3>

    <ul>
      <li>Ensure the game is closed</li>
      <li>Connect an external storage device</li>
      <li>
        Navigate to Program Files (x86), which is usually found in File Explorer
        - This PC - Local Disk (C:)
      </li>
      <li>
        Navigate to Steam - userdata - a folder named after your Steam ID -
        2246340 - remote
      </li>
      <li>
        The win64_save folder is your game's saved data. Copy the entire folder
        to an external storage device
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>To restore a backup:</h3>

    <p>
      <b>Note:</b> If Steam Cloud is enabled,<strong>
        synchronisation conflicts may occur when restoring an older backup.</strong
      > Pay attention to any synchronisation prompts to avoid overwriting the save
      you intend to keep.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Ensure Monster Hunter Wilds is closed</li>

      <li>
        Disable Steam Cloud for Monster Hunter Wilds to avoid synchronisation
        conflicts (Open Steam - Library - Right-click Monster Hunter Wilds -
        Properties - Manage Cloud Settings - Ensure the "Enable Steam Cloud"
        toggle is disabled)
      </li>

      <li>Close Steam completely</li>

      <li>Connect the external storage device that contains the backup</li>

      <li>Navigate to the original save location</li>

      <li>
        Make a separate copy of your current win64_save folder in case you need
        to revert
      </li>

      <li>Replace the existing win64_save folder with your backed-up copy</li>

      <li>Launch the game, and check whether your progress loads correctly</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      When satisfied that the restored save works, you may re-enable Steam
      Cloud. However, you may be prompted about synchronisation conflicts. Read
      the prompts carefully to determine which save data you would like to be
      used.
    </p>
  </p>
</HeadLayout>
